{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_7d8678b137277b1f3874b1c7d5de25001dad27d72211fcff0b4c49c899459906"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Several integrations (AdaL, Aether, Agent Layer, Agentlink) are documented as beta and guidance-only: they write instruction files telling agents to use `tokenjuice wrap`, but do not intercept or replace terminal command output."}],"claim_ids":["clm_7d8678b137277b1f3874b1c7d5de25001dad27d72211fcff0b4c49c899459906"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","id":"pg_a8cdf5854bf652489da6a44dd2ac25d0","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vincentkoc-tokenjuice-docs-agentlink-integration-md-43a621ab06ef-a44dd2ac25d0.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_379dce5b7b9f5e6fb357e3552fb9afee"],"title":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice/docs/agentlink-integration.md @ 43a621ab06ef","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_12ea4a9761d815c0765fd9fb08e4dadbc95984e948a10978c95757180111e2e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI ships install/uninstall commands covering many agent hosts (including claude-code, codex, cursor, droid, copilot-cli), plus `doctor hooks` to check installed wiring and `doctor <host>` for a single integration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1b39b28e54f0344981ba85b66ddae5196177e6fed2c9fd316f57c39ace214af2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented integrations include Claude Code, CodeBuddy, Codex CLI, Cursor, Droid, GitHub Copilot CLI, and OpenClaw, each with an install command and hook/settings file location; OpenClaw support is bundled on the OpenClaw side and requires version 2026.4.22 or newer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1baf119d122b6de0611f2750b4801eb0a8641396e85f7ac74c4570636c8325f6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Host adapters apply a narrow safe-inventory policy: exact file-content reads stay raw, standalone repository inventory commands can be compacted, and unsafe mixed command sequences stay raw."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2aed415c8051e4b113c13b67c42346d05963b8fe58f50e20418c8295f6c44335"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI has three surfaces: `reduce` compacts existing text, `wrap` runs a command and compacts its observed output, and `reduce-json` provides a stable machine protocol for host adapters."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6262ae9de4ca0a4a1de7af14adff2f8b3676b54349a88b1ffff12f6003abc0f4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"tokenjuice is distributed via npm (`npm install -g tokenjuice`), pnpm, yarn global, and a Homebrew tap (`brew tap vincentkoc/tap; brew install tokenjuice`)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6820141872b1c8bab63a6b6b95af564a3f20a45d0b1067f322c30de42590e81f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project's stated status is a usable foundation for token reduction with diagnostics and a growing reducer set, now focused on deeper coverage and tuning."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b1c93925aca75d3c71781f7ffffa0a712075c9edddc351d57440f94fc21e496"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: Homebrew publication is owned by the Tokenjuice workflow in the canonical vincentkoc/homebrew-tap repository, and release maintainers dispatch it manually with the published tag until GitHub App automation lands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_798e8d56af8265e89e755d8d3222777cddce51f50f3fbfb205a6d277e166807e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Statistics use bounded metadata segments, support paging via --limit and a returned --cursor, report partial coverage, and can be disabled with TOKENJUICE_STATS=off or --no-stats; artifact retention is opt-in via --store."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8563deaaa301352baa4c73d3913786e76f8ec4a7f11e3a00d0f27e1c028ed95e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`reduce-json` reads JSON from stdin or a file and always writes JSON to stdout; the documented payload includes fields such as toolName, command, argv, combinedText, and exitCode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9236783652fb6073241ccd2c6160a2b6df79cef51773d2d8df8258f43f40b27f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"tokenjuice is described as a deterministic output compactor for terminal-heavy agent workflows: it observes command output after execution and returns a smaller payload built from rule-driven reducers instead of the full terminal text."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a61f3305173e2669b96b8618c2fcb64b7a5f9cb5f05c4cafdfdbf3a027eaa995"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The design keeps command semantics untouched, exposes raw output only via explicit --raw/--full or opt-in artifact storage, keeps rules as inspectable JSON, and keeps host integrations as thin wrappers around one shared core reducer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c4076aa8303a4fe2a278b2ee6ba86f0fdb8a1d32183dc38d1d7b2ce591ba1fff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The reduction engine is rule-driven: built-in JSON rules live in src/rules, user overrides in ~/.config/tokenjuice/rules, and project overrides in .tokenjuice/rules, with later layers overriding earlier ones by rule id."}],"claim_ids":["clm_12ea4a9761d815c0765fd9fb08e4dadbc95984e948a10978c95757180111e2e4","clm_1b39b28e54f0344981ba85b66ddae5196177e6fed2c9fd316f57c39ace214af2","clm_1baf119d122b6de0611f2750b4801eb0a8641396e85f7ac74c4570636c8325f6","clm_2aed415c8051e4b113c13b67c42346d05963b8fe58f50e20418c8295f6c44335","clm_6262ae9de4ca0a4a1de7af14adff2f8b3676b54349a88b1ffff12f6003abc0f4","clm_6820141872b1c8bab63a6b6b95af564a3f20a45d0b1067f322c30de42590e81f","clm_6b1c93925aca75d3c71781f7ffffa0a712075c9edddc351d57440f94fc21e496","clm_798e8d56af8265e89e755d8d3222777cddce51f50f3fbfb205a6d277e166807e","clm_8563deaaa301352baa4c73d3913786e76f8ec4a7f11e3a00d0f27e1c028ed95e","clm_9236783652fb6073241ccd2c6160a2b6df79cef51773d2d8df8258f43f40b27f","clm_a61f3305173e2669b96b8618c2fcb64b7a5f9cb5f05c4cafdfdbf3a027eaa995","clm_c4076aa8303a4fe2a278b2ee6ba86f0fdb8a1d32183dc38d1d7b2ce591ba1fff"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","created_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24","id":"pg_be587d107160547ba2866fce4d862a3a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vincentkoc-tokenjuice-readme-md-43a621ab06ef-6fce4d862a3a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f20f33d559455ba9a3052f838a3bca7c"],"title":"vincentkoc/tokenjuice/README.md @ 43a621ab06ef","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:22Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4bbba800506b49f39200b67746384f24"}
